.TH SDL_strlwr 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_strlwr \- Convert a string to lowercase.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "char * SDL_strlwr(char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR WARNING :
Regardless of system locale, this will only convert ASCII values \(aqA\(aq through \(aqZ\(aq to lowercase\[char46]
.PP
This function operates on a null-terminated string of bytes--even if it is malformed UTF-8!--and converts ASCII characters \(aqA\(aq through \(aqZ\(aq to their lowercase equivalents in-place, returning the original
.BR str
pointer\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I str
the string to convert in-place\[char46] Can not be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the
.BR str
pointer passed into this function\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_strupr (3)
